1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,719
Welcome to Atomic Education.

2
00:00:02,781 --> 00:00:10,211
This lesson was written by the Atomic teaching team to help you learn Cambridge Lower Secondary Science with confidence.

3
00:00:10,211 --> 00:00:10,948
Let's begin!

4
00:00:12,010 --> 00:00:14,773
Welcome to Unit 3: Variation and Inheritance.

5
00:00:15,835 --> 00:00:20,563
Malaria, spread by mosquitoes, kills more than half a million people a year.

6
00:00:20,563 --> 00:00:26,643
Insecticide-treated bed nets protect sleepers, but they have become less effective over time. Why?

7
00:00:26,643 --> 00:00:28,915
By the end of this unit, you'll know.

8
00:00:29,976 --> 00:00:33,047
Inside the nucleus of every cell are chromosomes,

9
00:00:33,047 --> 00:00:36,547
carrying the genetic information that controls the cell.

10
00:00:36,547 --> 00:00:42,872
Each species has a set number: humans have 23 pairs, 46 in all, including one pair of sex chromosomes.

11
00:00:42,872 --> 00:00:45,267
Camels have 74, and fruit flies just 8!

12
00:00:46,329 --> 00:00:49,767
Each chromosome carries hundreds or thousands of genes.

13
00:00:49,767 --> 00:00:55,233
A gene is a section of DNA that controls a characteristic, or trait, such as eye colour.

14
00:00:55,233 --> 00:01:00,391
Genes can have different forms: one form may give a cat long fur, another short fur.

15
00:01:01,453 --> 00:01:04,032
Chromosomes are made of DNA and proteins.

16
00:01:04,032 --> 00:01:08,331
A DNA molecule has two strands twisted like a ladder: a double helix.

17
00:01:08,331 --> 00:01:13,489
When cells divide, the chromosomes are copied, so each new cell gets a complete set.

18
00:01:14,550 --> 00:01:17,805
Scientists found DNA long before they understood it.

19
00:01:17,805 --> 00:01:21,797
In 1869, Friedrich Miescher found a substance he called nuclein.

20
00:01:21,797 --> 00:01:27,139
Albrecht Kossel named DNA and RNA, and Phoebus Levene discovered DNA's building blocks.

21
00:01:28,201 --> 00:01:34,219
In 1944, Avery, MacLeod and McCarty showed that DNA, not protein, carries hereditary information.

22
00:01:34,219 --> 00:01:39,316
Then in 1953, James Watson and Francis Crick discovered the double helix structure.

23
00:01:40,377 --> 00:01:47,194
Their model relied on Rosalind Franklin's X-ray images: science develops as people build on each other's work.

24
00:01:47,194 --> 00:01:50,755
In 2003, the Human Genome Project mapped all human genes,

25
00:01:50,755 --> 00:01:54,440
helping to find genes behind disorders like cystic fibrosis.
